WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.199
Write a math

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:02.460
proof using TypeScript's

00:00:02.272 --> 00:00:03.144
type checker

00:00:03.678 --> 00:00:04.491
Lean lets you

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:05.564
prove mathematical

00:00:05.376 --> 00:00:06.366
propositions

00:00:06.414 --> 00:00:07.593
and its verifier

00:00:07.404 --> 00:00:08.418
is really just

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.090
a type checker

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:10.800
propositions are types

00:00:10.612 --> 00:00:11.661
and proofs are

00:00:11.473 --> 00:00:12.274
values

00:00:12.814 --> 00:00:14.099
Niklas Gruhn shows

00:00:13.911 --> 00:00:15.325
TypeScript's type system

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.245
is similar enough

00:00:16.092 --> 00:00:16.681
that you can

00:00:16.493 --> 00:00:18.085
prove simple propositions

00:00:17.897 --> 00:00:18.674
right in it

00:00:19.214 --> 00:00:20.039
His pitch

00:00:20.193 --> 00:00:21.407
LLMs write code

00:00:21.219 --> 00:00:21.820
fast

00:00:21.985 --> 00:00:23.789
Lean automates verification

00:00:23.636 --> 00:00:24.579
and that pairing

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:25.475
could bring stronger

00:00:25.287 --> 00:00:26.631
guarantees to everyday

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:27.456
software too

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.004
Full story on

00:00:28.815 --> 00:00:29.711
the dashboard
